# Cantilever with a load at the tip

The deflection at the free end is $\delta = P L^3 / (3 E I)$ and the fixed-end moment is $M = P L$.

## Inputs
P: 20 kN | load at the free end
L: 3 m | length
I: 160000 cm^4 | second moment of area
E: 30 GPa | modulus of elasticity

## Results
delta: P * L^3 / (3 * E * I) -> mm | tip deflection
theta: P * L^2 / (2 * E * I) | tip rotation, in radians
M_max: P * L -> kN*m | moment at the fixed end

for k in 1..3:
    d_k: k * P * L^3 / (3 * E * I) -> mm | tip deflection for a load of $k P$
